---
/**
 * Pins the colour scheme to light.
 *
 * Starlight's own provider reads localStorage and prefers-color-scheme and sets
 * `data-theme` accordingly. Starlight treats dark as the :root default and light as
 * `[data-theme='light']`, so the attribute has to be set to light rather than simply
 * left off.
 *
 * `StarlightThemeProvider.updatePickers` is kept as a no-op: ThemeSelect renders
 * nothing here, but the global is part of Starlight's inline contract and anything
 * still calling it should not throw.
 */
---

{/* Inlined rather than bundled so the theme is set before first paint. */}
<script is:inline>
	document.documentElement.dataset.theme = 'light';
	window.StarlightThemeProvider = { updatePickers() {} };
</script>
